<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Casebound report: {{ scenario }}</title>
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #ffffff;
  --ink: #1b1f24;
  --muted: #5b6470;
  --line: #d8dee6;
  --panel: #f6f8fa;
  --accept: #1a7f37;
  --reject: #b42318;
  --reject-bg: #fbe9e7;
  --link: #0a4fa0;
  --chip: #eaeef3;
}
/* Dark mode follows the reader's OS preference. The report stays self-contained:
   these are only token overrides, no external asset is fetched. */
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --bg: #0d1117;
    --ink: #e6edf3;
    --muted: #9198a1;
    --line: #30363d;
    --panel: #161b22;
    --accept: #3fb950;
    --reject: #f85149;
    --reject-bg: #3d1614;
    --link: #4493f8;
    --chip: #21262d;
  }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  color: var(--ink);
  background: var(--bg);
}
.wrap { max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 24px 64px; }
header.masthead { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-bottom: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
header.masthead h1 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
header.masthead .tagline { color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
.guarantee { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 18px; margin: 20px 0; }
.guarantee p { margin: 0; }
.summary { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
.stat { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px 14px; min-width: 120px; }
.stat .n { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; }
.stat .k { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
.notice { border-left: 4px solid var(--link); background: var(--panel); padding: 12px 16px; margin: 18px 0; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; }
section { margin: 36px 0; }
section > h2 { font-size: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 6px; }
.lead { color: var(--muted); margin-top: -4px; }
/* Wide tables (the timeline, the indicators) scroll sideways on a narrow screen
   instead of overflowing the page. */
.tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13.5px; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 7px 9px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
th { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; color: var(--muted); }
td.mono, code, .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }
td.when { white-space: nowrap; }
a { color: var(--link); }
.chip { display: inline-block; background: var(--chip); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; padding: 1px 8px; font-size: 11.5px; margin: 1px 2px; white-space: nowrap; }
.chip.tech { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }
.claim { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--accept); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 12px 0; }
.claim .statement { font-size: 15.5px; }
.claim .cites { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
.audit { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--reject); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 12px 0; }
.audit .why { margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px; }
.badge { display: inline-block; border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 7px; font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 600; }
.badge.reject { background: var(--reject-bg); color: var(--reject); }
.badge.drop { background: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); }
.empty { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
.appendix .event { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 12px 0; }
.appendix .event:target { border-color: var(--link); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(10, 79, 160, 0.18); }
.appendix .event h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
.appendix dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr; gap: 2px 12px; margin: 0; }
.appendix dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
.appendix dd { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; word-break: break-word; }
.chip.ep { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }
.chip.ioc { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }
.chip.iocty { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--muted); }
.episode { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--link); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 12px 0; }
.episode h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 14px; }
.episode .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.episode .members { font-size: 12.5px; }
footer { margin-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 14px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header class="masthead">
  <h1>Casebound investigation report</h1>
  <p class="tagline">Scenario: {{ scenario }}. Source tool: {{ source_tool }}. Narrative: {{ model_label }}.</p>
</header>

<div class="guarantee">
  <p><strong>The guarantee.</strong> No factual claim appears in the narrative below unless it
  resolves to a real, deterministically extracted timeline event by id and its asserted facts
  (time, principal, action, object) are consistent with that event. The deterministic timeline
  and appendix are the source of truth; the language model never decides what is true.</p>
</div>

<div class="summary">
  <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ stats.events }}</div><div class="k">Timeline events</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ stats.hosts }}</div><div class="k">Hosts</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ stats.techniques }}</div><div class="k">ATT&amp;CK techniques</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ stats.accepted }}</div><div class="k">Verified claims</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ stats.rejected }}</div><div class="k">Rejected claims</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ stats.episodes }}</div><div class="k">Activity episodes</div></div>
  <div class="stat"><div class="n">{{ stats.iocs }}</div><div class="k">Indicators</div></div>
</div>

{% if observed_techniques %}
<p class="lead">Observed techniques:
{% for tid in observed_techniques %}<span class="chip tech">{{ tid }}</span>{% endfor %}
</p>
{% endif %}

<section id="narrative">
  <h2>Verified narrative</h2>
  {% if no_model %}
  <div class="notice">
    <strong>No language model configured.</strong> This is the deterministic report
    (the no-model path). The verified narrative is an optional layer that defaults to a
    local model so evidence never leaves the host. With no model configured, Casebound
    still produces the full normalized timeline, the ATT&amp;CK tags, and the evidence
    appendix below. Configure a local model to add the verified narrative.
  </div>
  {% elif accepted %}
  <p class="lead">Each statement is rendered from fields the verifier checked against the cited
  event, never from the model's free prose. Every citation links to its event in the appendix.</p>
  {% for claim in accepted %}
  <div class="claim">
    <div class="statement">{{ claim.statement }}</div>
    <div class="cites">Backing evidence:
      <a href="#event-{{ claim.backing.id }}" class="mono">{{ claim.backing.short }}</a>
      {% if claim.context_citations %}<span style="color:var(--muted);"> (also cited for context:
        {% for c in claim.context_citations %}<a href="#event-{{ c.id }}" class="mono">{{ c.short }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">The model proposed no claim that survived verification.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="audit">
  <h2>Rejected-claims audit</h2>
  <p class="lead">Every claim the verifier rejected is recorded here for transparency, with the
  reason it failed. A dropped claim never reached the narrative above.</p>
  {% if audit %}
  {% for entry in audit %}
  <div class="audit">
    <div>
      <span class="badge reject">{{ entry.reason }}</span>
      {% if entry.dropped %}<span class="badge drop">dropped</span>{% endif %}
      <span class="mono" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;">round {{ entry.round_index }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="why">Model draft: {{ entry.claim_text }}</div>
    <div class="why" style="color:var(--muted);">Reason: {{ entry.detail }}</div>
    {% if entry.citations %}
    <div class="cites">Cited:
      {% for c in entry.citations %}<code>{{ c }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">No claims were rejected.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="timeline">
  <h2>Deterministic timeline</h2>
  <p class="lead">Every event normalized to the canonical schema and tagged with ATT&amp;CK
  deterministically. Each id links to its full record in the appendix.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Time (UTC)</th><th>Host</th><th>Principal</th><th>Action</th><th>Object</th><th>ATT&amp;CK</th><th>Event</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for ev in timeline %}
      <tr>
        <td class="when mono">{{ ev.datetime }}</td>
        <td>{{ ev.host or "" }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ ev.principal or "" }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ ev.action }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ ev.object or "" }}</td>
        <td>{% for tid in ev.techniques %}<span class="chip tech">{{ tid }}</span>{% endfor %}</td>
        <td><a href="#event-{{ ev.event_id }}" class="mono">{{ ev.short_id }}</a></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="episodes">
  <h2>Activity episodes</h2>
  <p class="lead">Events grouped into episodes by host, principal, and time proximity. Each
  episode is one actor's coherent run of activity on one host; its id tags every member
  event so the timeline can be read as a sequence of episodes.</p>
  {% if episodes %}
  {% for ep in episodes %}
  <div class="episode">
    <h3 class="mono">{{ ep.episode_id }}</h3>
    <div class="meta">
      Host: {{ ep.host if ep.host is not none else "unattributed" }}.
      Principal: <span class="mono">{{ ep.principal if ep.principal is not none else "unattributed" }}</span>.
      {{ ep.event_count }} event(s) from {{ ep.start }} to {{ ep.end }}.
    </div>
    <div class="members">Events:
      {% for m in ep.members %}<a href="#event-{{ m.id }}" class="mono">{{ m.short }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">No episodes were formed.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="iocs">
  <h2>Indicators of compromise</h2>
  <p class="lead">Indicators extracted from the events and defanged for safe handling: IPs and
  domains have their dots bracketed, hashes and paths are listed verbatim. Each indicator links
  to the events that reference it.</p>
  {% if iocs %}
  <div class="tablewrap">
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Type</th><th>Indicator (defanged)</th><th>Events</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for ioc in iocs %}
      <tr>
        <td><span class="chip iocty">{{ ioc.ioc_type }}</span></td>
        <td class="mono">{{ ioc.defanged }}</td>
        <td>{% for e in ioc.events %}<a href="#event-{{ e.id }}" class="mono">{{ e.short }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">No indicators were extracted.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section id="appendix" class="appendix">
  <h2>Evidence appendix</h2>
  <p class="lead">The full canonical record for every event, with its source provenance for audit.
  This is the deterministic source of truth the narrative is fenced to.</p>
  {% for ev in appendix %}
  <div class="event" id="event-{{ ev.event_id }}">
    <h3 class="mono">{{ ev.event_id }}</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>message</dt><dd>{{ ev.message }}</dd>
      <dt>datetime</dt><dd class="mono">{{ ev.datetime }}</dd>
      <dt>timestamp_desc</dt><dd>{{ ev.timestamp_desc }}</dd>
      <dt>host</dt><dd>{{ ev.host or "" }}</dd>
      <dt>principal</dt><dd class="mono">{{ ev.principal or "" }}</dd>
      <dt>action</dt><dd class="mono">{{ ev.action }}</dd>
      <dt>object</dt><dd class="mono">{{ ev.object or "" }}</dd>
      <dt>source</dt><dd>{{ ev.source_tool }} / {{ ev.source_artifact }}</dd>
      {% if ev.attack_techniques %}
      <dt>attack_techniques</dt><dd>{% for t in ev.attack_techniques %}<span class="chip tech">{{ t.technique_id }}</span> <span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:11.5px;">({{ t.mapping_source }})</span>{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if ev.episode_id %}
      <dt>episode</dt><dd><span class="chip ep">{{ ev.episode_id }}</span></dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if ev.iocs %}
      <dt>iocs</dt><dd>{% for i in ev.iocs %}<span class="chip ioc">{{ i.defanged }}</span> <span class="iocty">{{ i.type }}</span>{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if ev.details %}
      <dt>details</dt><dd>{% for k, v in ev.details %}<div><span style="color:var(--muted);">{{ k }}:</span> <span class="mono">{{ v }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>provenance</dt><dd>{% for ref in ev.provenance %}<span class="mono">{{ ref }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<footer>
  Generated by Casebound, offline, from synthetic evidence. The deterministic timeline, the
  ATT&amp;CK tags, and this appendix regenerate from a clean clone with no API keys. Citation
  accuracy is 1.0 by construction: every claim above links to a field-consistent event.
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
